sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant U as User (Browser)
    participant APP as login.js / customer.js
    participant AUTH as auth.js fetch wrapper
    participant LS as localStorage
    participant API as Backend API (Node.js)

    note over U, API: FRONTEND REQUEST RESPONSE AND TOKEN REFRESH SECTION

    rect rgb(240, 248, 255)
        note right of APP: 1. Feature Function Sends Request
        U->>APP: Trigger action (login, load accounts, submit form)
        APP->>AUTH: fetch(getApiUrl(endpoint), init)
        AUTH->>AUTH: Detect API request and endpoint type
        AUTH->>AUTH: Attach credentials: include
        AUTH->>AUTH: Attach Authorization: Bearer token (for protected endpoints)
        AUTH->>API: HTTP request
    end

    rect rgb(255, 250, 240)
        note right of AUTH: 2. Normal Response Path
        API-->>AUTH: 2xx / 4xx / 5xx response
        alt Not 401 or auth endpoint
            AUTH-->>APP: Return response directly
            APP->>APP: await res.json()
            APP->>APP: Update DOM message/table/cards from response payload
        end
    end

    rect rgb(245, 255, 245)
        note right of AUTH: 3. 401 Auto-Refresh Retry Path
        API-->>AUTH: 401 on protected endpoint
        AUTH->>API: POST /auth/refresh (cookie-based)
        alt Refresh success
            API-->>AUTH: 200 { token, role }
            AUTH->>LS: localStorage.setItem("token", token)
            AUTH->>LS: localStorage.setItem("role", role)
            AUTH->>API: Retry original request with new bearer token
            API-->>AUTH: Retried response
            AUTH-->>APP: Return retried response
            APP->>APP: Parse JSON and continue normal UI update
        else Refresh failed
            AUTH->>LS: Save sessionExpiredMessage
            AUTH->>LS: Clear token + role
            AUTH-->>U: Redirect to ../login.html
        end
    end
